{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Take the firepan.</b> Since they said that the cause of those who were burned was on account of the burning of the incense, which brought about the death of the people of HaShem, therefore He showed them that even though the incense was offered outside its time and outside its place — on the contrary, it held back the death from Israel. And through this they will vindicate that all is the deed of HaShem, for He brings death to the guilty without any intermediary. And our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Shabbat 89a) that this matter they learned from the [evil] inclination [yetzer] when it went up to receive the Torah."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:10:34.992254463Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}